            <ArticleTitle>[Age-related features of neurohumoral effects of dopamine activity on the cardiovascular system in elderly people].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Determined the decrease in dopamine activity with age, that contributes to the pathogenesis of hypertension, abdominal obesity, the development of left ventricular hypertrophy. The article presents information describing the age-sensitive regulation of the cardiovascular system in elderly people, confirming the influence of the activity of dopamine receptors in the development of age pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
